PackageSummary: <text>
Taurino is an asynchronous, cross-platform web-based GUI
framework for Python, powered by Rust, Tokio, Tao, Wry,
and PyO3.
</text>

PackageDescription: <text>
Taurino is a Python GUI framework providing native desktop
windows, embedded webviews, asynchronous execution, and
inter-process communication through a Rust-based runtime.

The framework integrates Tao for native window management,
Wry for embedded webviews, Tokio for asynchronous execution,
and PyO3 for Python and Rust interoperability.

The Python package uses Maturin as its build backend and
exposes the native extension module taurino._taurino.

Its declared Python runtime dependencies include Pydantic,
Taunicorn, and MessagePack.

Taurino is distributed under the MIT OR Apache-2.0
dual-license expression.
</text>

